    "knowledge_point": "Evaluating Definite Integrals",
    "problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
    "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x).$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5x}\\cdot 5=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/5$ | ${e}^{4}/5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{e/5}^{{e}^{4}/5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{1/2}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {\\sqrt{u}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
